{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013WMt9GT17ShnV6sUiN3mcL","type":"tool_result","content":"71:  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n85:    - \"Print each fan-out lineage's command with fanout-run.cjs --preview, which builds the commands and writes nothing.\"\n96:    default_halt_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"dry_run_halt\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"boundary\":\"{dry_run_boundary}\",\"step\":\"{step_name}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n98:  halt_hook_rule: \"Before executing any command, dispatch, edit, output, template write, append_to_jsonl, append_jsonl, log_event, mcp_tool, write, or git-index mutation in a step tagged with dry_run_boundary, emit event_policy.default_halt_event with that step's name and boundary to the terminal and halt; at step_fanout_spawn print the dry_run_halt the fan-out preview returned instead, when it returned one. This holds in both execution modes.\"\n163:  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n189:  # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n193:  packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n196:  config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n197:  state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n198:  findings_registry: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n199:  strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n200:  dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n201:  pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n202:  lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review.lock\"\n203:  prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n204:  iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n205:  iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n209:  delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n210:  delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n211:  review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n212:  resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n223:    on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet, so run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n227:  step_resolve_artifact_root:\n230:    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n233:        artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n234:        artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n236:        artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n242:        - artifact_dir: \"Resolved review packet directory for this target\"\n245:  step_bind_reducer_artifact_arg:\n247:    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n250:        reducer_artifact_arg: \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\"\n255:  step_bind_convergence_write_arg:\n257:    note: \"step_graph_convergence runs on a dry run as a preview. A live run passes --record-blocked-stop, which makes convergence.cjs append a real row on a BLOCKED decision. A dry run writes nothing, so it passes --read-only instead, which also keeps the script from persisting the graph snapshot or appending its observability event.\"\n266:  step_fanout_dry_run_preview:\n269:    skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent or no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n272:      A fan-out dry run halts at step_apply_lifecycle_request under --restart and at the\n275:      prints. Write {review_focus} verbatim to {preview_input_dir}/fanout-review-focus.txt,\n276:      {review_target} verbatim to {preview_input_dir}/fanout-review-target.txt, an empty\n277:      {preview_input_dir}/fanout-review-scope.txt (empty means no seeded scope) and\n278:      {config.fanout_json} verbatim to {preview_input_dir}/fanout-config.json with the\n279:      file-write tool, never through a shell, under the same rules step_fanout_spawn\n280:      states, so nothing lands in {artifact_dir}. The command is step_fanout_spawn_cli's\n288:      is the runner's halt event for step_fanout_spawn, and when the halt lands there, print that\n291:      and frontier_scope come from the current packet. Before step_frontier_seed every\n294:      their digests differ from the real spawn's whenever step_fanout_scope_discovery finds files.\n296:      node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs \\\n299:        --review-focus-file \"{preview_input_dir}/fanout-review-focus.txt\" \\\n300:        --review-target-file \"{preview_input_dir}/fanout-review-target.txt\" \\\n302:        --review-scope-file \"{preview_input_dir}/fanout-review-scope.txt\" \\\n303:        --fanout-config-json-file \"{preview_input_dir}/fanout-config.json\" \\\n304:        --base-artifact-dir {artifact_dir} \\\n313:  step_apply_lifecycle_request:\n347:  step_reject_extend_with_fanout:\n349:    skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'completed-continue' or config.fanout is absent\"\n351:      A fan-out run jumps from step_fanout_spawn to phase_synthesis and never\n354:      combination here, before step_fanout_spawn, so no lineage spawns.\n357:    message: \"Usage error (extend-with-fanout): --extend extends a single-executor review run only. This config has fanout executors, so nothing was spawned and the run is unchanged.\"\n359:  step_reject_frontier_caps_with_fanout:\n361:    skip_when: \"frontier_max_depth and frontier_max_nodes are both unset or config.fanout is absent\"\n368:    message: \"Usage error (frontier-caps-with-fanout): --frontier-max-depth and --frontier-max-nodes apply to a single-executor review run only. This config has fanout executors, so nothing was spawned and the run is unchanged.\"\n370:  step_frontier_seed:\n373:    skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n376:      Fan-out jumps from step_fanout_spawn to phase_synthesis and never reaches\n377:      phase_init, so the seed runs here or not at all. fanout-run.cjs then splits\n385:      {artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json, one object per sub-target:\n388:      command. frontier-admit.cjs writes the node store, and fanout-run.cjs\n393:    command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n395:    optional_flags: \"When max_iterations_source != 'default', append `--max-iterations {max_iterations}`: this seed runs before step_fanout_root_config writes the root config, so without it the budget line reads the loop default instead of the bound value. When max_iterations_source == 'default', append nothing.\"\n400:  step_fanout_spawn:\n403:    skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n406:      isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n407:      This step runs before phase_init, so pass the raw review_focus. fanout-run.cjs\n409:      {review_focus} verbatim to {artifact_dir}/fanout-review-focus.txt, {review_target}\n410:      verbatim to {artifact_dir}/fanout-review-target.txt and {config.fanout_json} verbatim\n411:      to {artifact_dir}/fanout-config.json with the file-write tool, never through a shell:\n417:      self-invocation path. fanout-run.cjs owns the stack-only recursion guard for that\n419:      fanout-run.cjs owns every fan-out lineage, and each one needs a cli-* executor.\n428:      step_fanout_scope_discovery:\n431:          Fan-out never reaches phase_init, so step_scope_discovery would never run at the\n433:          Run step_scope_discovery's resolve rule for {review_target_type} here and bind\n435:          order, to {artifact_dir}/fanout-review-scope.txt with the file-write tool, never\n437:          an empty file as no seeded scope. fanout-run.cjs validates every line, hands the list\n440:          - review_scope_files: \"The discovered files, also written to {artifact_dir}/fanout-review-scope.txt\"\n441:      step_fanout_root_config:\n445:          Fan-out never reaches phase_init, so step_create_config never runs here, yet\n446:          step_update_config_status and a later --restart both read the root config. Write\n447:          it with step_create_config's template and populate map, the lineage_values below\n452:          fanout-run.cjs reads the lineage values below from this file and copies them into\n461:        populate_from: step_create_config\n467:          fanout: \"{config.fanout_json}\"\n469:      step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n471:        skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n473:          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs \\\n476:            --review-focus-file \"{artifact_dir}/fanout-review-focus.txt\" \\\n477:            --review-target-file \"{artifact_dir}/fanout-review-target.txt\" \\\n479:            --review-scope-file \"{artifact_dir}/fanout-review-scope.txt\" \\\n480:            --fanout-config-json-file \"{artifact_dir}/fanout-config.json\" \\\n481:            --base-artifact-dir {artifact_dir} \\\n498:      step_preflight_contract:\n506:          - extend_values: \"When extend is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), and extend_minutes when bound likewise. extend_minutes without extend, or extend with a lineage_mode other than auto or completed-continue, is a usage error. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock, with a usage error that names the flag.\"\n507:          - frontier_cap_values: \"When frontier_max_depth or frontier_max_nodes is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), else fail with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-value): --frontier-max-depth needs a positive integer' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Either one bound while depth_mode != 'expansive' fails with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-without-expansive): --frontier-max-depth only applies with --depth-mode=expansive' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock.\"\n510:      step_create_directories:\n515:      step_detect_resource_map:\n526:      step_migrate_legacy_review_state:\n557:        on_legacy_detected: \"Move only the review-specific whitelist, print LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED and leave unrelated scratch files untouched. Nothing is appended here: an append before session classification would create the state log and turn a fresh packet into a partial one, and the moved state log was written without the ledger, so the gateway refuses every append to it until step_classify_session.on_moved_legacy_state adopts it.\"\n561:          - migration_recorded: \"false; step_record_artifact_migration sets it once the migration row is appended\"\n576:      step_acquire_lock:\n584:        # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n586:          action: \"Every terminal halt after the acquire runs step_release_lock before it returns control\"\n595:      step_extend_completed_run:\n606:          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n607:          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n620:        on_fail: \"Exit 2 is a usage error, such as a run that is not complete: halt with that message through step_release_lock and leave the config untouched. Any other failure halts with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock.\"\n622:      step_snapshot_extended_review_report:\n637:        on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. Never overwrite an existing snapshot.\"\n639:      step_classify_session:\n651:        extension_rule: \"When extension_pending == true, step_extend_completed_run has just set status initialized and appended run_extended, so a synthesis_complete row followed by an extended row is consistent: classify as resume, never as invalid-state or completed-session.\"\n656:          - \"If lineage_mode == restart, step_apply_lifecycle_request archived the packet before the lock was taken, so session_state is fresh and on_fresh runs.\"\n662:          extension_override: \"When extension_pending == true, skip this append_jsonl: step_extend_completed_run already recorded the lifecycle action as run_extended, so the ledger carries one event per action. Keep lineage_mode completed-continue and skip_to phase_loop.\"\n690:                on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The old config is unreadable, so repair or archive the packet by hand.\"\n699:              on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. Never fall back to resume.\"\n702:              skip_to: step_create_config\n705:              release_lock: step_release_lock\n708:          action: \"Nothing is archived here. step_apply_lifecycle_request archived the packet before the lock was taken, so a restart run reaches this step as fresh and continues as on_fresh.\"\n710:        note_live_branches: \"completed-continue is live through --extend=N: step_extend_completed_run reopens a completed run before classification, so it lands here as resume. The live modes are new, resume, restart and completed-continue. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n728:          open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n730:            GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n731:            [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n740:          release_lock: step_release_lock\n745:      step_scope_discovery:\n779:      step_order_dimensions:\n795:      step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n810:      step_normalize_review_focus:\n816:          fanout-run.cjs applies the same rule in code, so a fan-out lineage receives the same text.\n818:      step_resolve_session_id:\n828:      step_create_config:\n846:          # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n865:          # Null derives the run-wide node cap at admission as half the iteration budget, so the frontier cannot claim every iteration; the depth-1 seed answers only to the root-children cap but counts toward this one. A defaulted budget is resized from the seed by step_frontier_budget so the cap keeps room past depth 1; an explicit budget is kept as given and may leave none.\n881:      step_frontier_scope:\n888:          list step_scope_discovery recorded with git diff --name-only <range> --\n891:          too, after its own step_create_config, so its list is the same as every\n893:        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs scope --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n899:      step_frontier_seed:\n902:        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n903:        skip_reason: \"A fan-out lineage receives its share of the parent's seeded nodes from fanout-run.cjs; seeding again would duplicate them.\"\n906:          Decompose {review_target} and write {artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\n907:          exactly as the root step_frontier_seed describes, then run the command.\n911:        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n917:      step_frontier_budget:\n920:        skip_when: \"extension_pending == true or config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:44:15.101Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"71:  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n85:    - \"Print each fan-out lineage's command with fanout-run.cjs --preview, which builds the commands and writes nothing.\"\n96:    default_halt_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"dry_run_halt\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"boundary\":\"{dry_run_boundary}\",\"step\":\"{step_name}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n98:  halt_hook_rule: \"Before executing any command, dispatch, edit, output, template write, append_to_jsonl, append_jsonl, log_event, mcp_tool, write, or git-index mutation in a step tagged with dry_run_boundary, emit event_policy.default_halt_event with that step's name and boundary to the terminal and halt; at step_fanout_spawn print the dry_run_halt the fan-out preview returned instead, when it returned one. This holds in both execution modes.\"\n163:  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n189:  # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n193:  packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n196:  config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n197:  state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n198:  findings_registry: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n199:  strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n200:  dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n201:  pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n202:  lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review.lock\"\n203:  prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n204:  iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n205:  iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n209:  delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n210:  delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n211:  review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n212:  resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n223:    on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the pack