 | system-deep-loop c=0.8737 u=0.16 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: sk-code c=0.8621 cmd=- pol=- || 3: command-doctor-deep-loop c=0.82\n107\tN8 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | sk-code c=0.9361 u=0.12 route/single/sk-code-review cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: system-deep-loop c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-doc c=0.82\n108\tN10 [exit 0 live] n=1 amb=false | system-deep-loop c=0.8573 u=0.12 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill\n109\tN12 [exit 0 live] n=0 amb=false | NONE\n110\tN13 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | sk-doc c=0.95 u=0.12 route/single/sk-create-readme cmd=/create:readme pol=start kind=skill || 2: system-spec-kit c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: mcp-tooling c=0.82\n111\tN14 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | sk-code c=0.9002 u=0.12 route/single/sk-code-review cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: system-deep-loop c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-doc c=0.82\n112\tN15 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | system-deep-loop c=0.8525 u=0.16 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: system-spec-kit c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-code c=0.82\n113\tA2 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | sk-code c=0.859 u=0.22 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: mcp-tooling c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-doc c=0.82\n114\tA7 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | sk-code c=0.859 u=0.22 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: mcp-tooling c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-doc c=0.82\n115\tH3a [exit 0 live] n=1 amb=false | command-speckit-ai-council c=0.8844 u=0.12 -/-/- cmd=/speckit:ai-council pol=ask kind=command\n116\tH4 [exit 0 live] n=0 amb=false | NONE\n117\tH5 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=true | sk-code c=0.95 u=0.16 route/single/sk-code-review cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: sk-doc c=0.95 cmd=- pol=- || 3: system-deep-loop c=0.82\n118\tH3b [exit 0 live] n=1 amb=false | system-deep-loop c=0.82 u=0.16 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill FLOORED\n119\tK1 [exit 0 live] n=1 amb=false | sk-prompt c=0.8217 u=0.12 -/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill\n120\tK2 [exit 0 live] n=0 amb=false | NONE\n121\tK3 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | system-deep-loop c=0.82 u=0.2 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill FLOORED || 2: cli-external-orchestration c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: system-spec-kit c=0.82\n122\tK5 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | sk-code c=0.9023 u=0.12 route/single/sk-code-review cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: system-deep-loop c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-doc c=0.82\n123\tK6 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=true | system-spec-kit c=0.95 u=0.16 -/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: sk-code c=0.9003 cmd=- pol=- || 3: system-deep-loop c=0.82\n124\tN7 [exit 0 live] n=1 amb=false | command-doctor-deep-loop c=0.8 u=0.34 -/-/- cmd=/doctor:deep-loop pol=run kind=command\n125\tD1 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | system-deep-loop c=0.9487 u=0.12 route/single/review cmd=/deep:review pol=ask kind=skill || 2: sk-code c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: command-doctor-deep-loop c=0.8\n126\tV7 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=true | sk-doc c=0.95 u=0.16 route/single/sk-create-manual-testing-playbook cmd=/create:manual-testing-playbook pol=start kind=skill || 2: system-deep-loop c=0.95 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-code c=0.95\n127\tA3 [exit 0 live] n=2 amb=false | system-deep-loop c=0.82 u=0.2 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill FLOORED || 2: sk-doc c=0.82 cmd=- pol=-\n128\t```\n129\t\n130\tWhat the block shows, by the `group` field in the probe file:\n131\t- **gain** (V6, H1a, H1b, E1, E3): five explicit loop asks, five `cmd=-`. V6, H1a and H1b already route to one mode. E1 and E3 defer.\n132\t- **stage-one** (R2, V2, V4, H7, H10): five explicit loop asks where the hub never tops.\n133\t- **lose** (R7): depth wording only, and it prints `cmd=/deep:research pol=ask`.\n134\t- **lose-n9** (N9): a summary of a past run that names \"deep research\" and prints `cmd=/deep:research pol=ask`.\n135\t- **no-gain** (V3, V8, V5, R2b, R3, R3b, R6, A1, A4, A8, H6, H8, H9): depth wording only, and no deep command today.\n136\t- **keep** (R1 to X2): named, typed or continue requests, seventeen rows, every one with its deep command.\n137\t- **negative** (N1 to H5): seventeen rows that ask for no loop.\n138\t- **drift** (H3b, K1, K2, K3, K5, K6) and **near-miss** (N7, D1, V7, A3): the rows the drift and corpus work aim at.\n139\t\n140\tThe 84-probe accuracy figures and the corpus run sit in `scratch/routing-analysis.md` section 2. This packet does not restate them as measured.\n141\t<!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n142\t\n143\t---\n144\t\n145\t<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n146\t## 3. SCOPE\n147\t\n148\t### In Scope\n149\t- Change the deep-loop command gate in `command-attach.ts` so it opens on an explicit loop ask and not on depth wording. Also let one mode cue resolve a deferred hub route when the prompt asks for the loop.\n150\t- Score explicit loop wording beside a research or review cue at stage one in `explicit.ts`, so the hub can top on a loop ask that never says \"deep\". Depth words do not score there.\n151\t- Add an \"Offer From an Advisor Brief\" section to both deep presentation files, with a pointer step in both command documents. The section covers one question, a flag table and `:auto` on a yes.\n152\t- Move the deep setup forms to the question tool with a recommended option, and make the finished-run and stuck-run messages name `--extend=N`, `--restart` and `/doctor:deep-loop`.\n153\t- Clear the drift between the advisor, the hub and the mode packets. Add the six single-probe misses as corpus near-miss rows, and replace the three deep-family holdout rows with fresh ones.\n154\t\n155\t### Out of Scope\n156\t- A `proposedArgs` field on the recommendation. Decision D5 keeps the advisor carrying only the command and its policy.\n157\t- A new guard for N7, N9, D1, V7, H6 or A3. Decision D6 records them as near-miss rows instead.\n158\t- `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and the repo rules. The analysis proposes no change to them.\n159\t- New phrases in `hub-router.json` beyond the three loop-shaped aliases D8 names. The anchored tune rows pass and the holdout rows fail, so more anchors would fit the corpus without fixing the gap.\n160\t\n161\t### Files to Change\n162\t\n163\t| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n164\t|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n165\t| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | Explicit loop gate, mode cue for a deferred route, and the council words dropped from the depth list |\n166\t| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts` | Modify | Stage-one loop rule beside a research or review cue; drop the `several models` boost |\n167\t| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` | Modify | Gate cases for every loop-ask clause and the depth-only negatives |\n168\t| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/` | Regenerate | Rebuilt so the CLI shim serves the new code |\n169\t| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` | Modify | Six near-miss rows; three fresh deep-family holdout rows |\n170\t| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` | Regenerate | Recaptured after the code change |\n171\t| `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md`, `.skilled/commands/deep/review.md` | Modify | Step 0 pointer to the offer section |\n172\t| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt`, `deep-review-presentation.txt` | Modify | Offer section, question-tool setup, recommended options, Next Steps rows, `=` flag form |\n173\t| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml`, `deep-review.yaml` | Modify | Completed-packet message and `--extend` next step |\n174\t| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/` | Regenerate | Compiled contracts rebuilt from the edited sources |\n175\t| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md` | Modify | One sentence naming `/doctor:deep-loop` |\n176\t| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/hub-router.json`, `ROUTER.md`, `graph-metadata.json` | Modify | The three loop-shaped research aliases, then the derived intent signals and activation manifest |\n177\t| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md` | Modify | Depth triggers removed; Gate 2 line names the advisor CLI |\n178\t| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md` | Modify | Depth triggers removed; attached `:auto` form |\n179\t| `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/quick-reference.md` | Modify | `=` flag form in the example |\n180\t<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n181\t\n182\t---\n183\t\n184\t<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n185\t## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n186\tREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n187\t\n188\tEvery probe requirement is checked by rerunning `scratch/probes/probes-spec-baseline.json` through `scratch/probes/probe.mjs` and reading the top row of each id.\n189\t\n190\t### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n191\t\n192\t| ID | Requirement |\n193\t|----|-------------|\n194\t| REQ-001 | Plain loop asks gain the command row. The top row reads `system-deep-loop` with `cmd=/deep:review pol=ask` for V6, H1a and E3, and `cmd=/deep:research pol=ask` for H1b and E1. Each prints `cmd=-` today. |\n195\t| REQ-002 | Depth-only requests carry no deep command. R7 prints `cmd=-` where it prints `cmd=/deep:research` today. V3, V8, V5, R2b, R3, R3b, R6, A1, A4, A8, H6, H8 and H9 carry no `/deep:*` command in any of their three rows. V5 (\"do a thorough code review\") keeps `sk-code` on `sk-code-review` as its top row. |\n196\t| REQ-003 | Named, typed and continue requests keep their command. R1, R5, V1, E2, E4, E5, E6, F3, F4, F5, F6, F8, F12, F13, H1e, X1 and X2 print the same `/deep:*` command and `pol=ask` as the baseline block. |\n197\t| REQ-004 | The negatives do not change. N1, N2, N3, N4, N5, N6, N8, N10, N12, N13, N14, N15, A2, A7, H3a, H4 and H5 print the same top skill and the same `cmd=` value as the baseline block. |\n198\t| REQ-005 | The offer is taught where the AI reads it. Both deep presentation files carry an `### Offer From an Advisor Brief` section. It asks one question through the runtime question tool. Option A is recommended and runs `:auto` with the composed flags plus `--spec-folder=<the Gate 3 answer>`. Option B runs `:confirm`. Option C is no loop. The executor is native unless the request names a `cli-*` executor or a model. Fan-out appears only when two or more executors or models are named, or independent takes are asked for. `research.md` and `review.md` each carry a step 0 that points at the section. |\n199\t| REQ-006 | The gate change is tested and served. `command-attach.vitest.ts` holds a passing case for each loop-ask clause and a passing `undefined` case for each depth word. The whole advisor vitest suite passes. `dist` is rebuilt, so the probe run prints `live` for every row. |\n200\t| REQ-007 | The command edits stay consistent. `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check` and `validate-command-references.cjs` both pass. The compiled contracts under `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/` are regenerated from the edited sources. |\n201\t\n202\t### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n203\t\n204\t| ID | Requirement |\n205\t|----|-------------|\n206\t| REQ-008 | Explicit loop wording beside a research or review cue scores at stage one, and depth wording does not. The probe rerun records the top row of R2, V2, V4, H7 and H10. Fusion decides the winner, so each id's outcome is recorded rather than required. No id in REQ-004 changes its top skill. |\n207\t| REQ-009 | Finished and stuck runs name their way forward. The completed-packet message in `deep-research.yaml` names `--extend=N` and `--restart`. Both presentation files' Next Steps tables gain an `--extend=N` row and a `/doctor:deep-loop --scope=<mode>` row. Both YAML `next_steps` lists gain the `--extend=N` line. |\n208\t| REQ-010 | Setup runs through the question tool. Step 6 of both presentation files names the question tool in `.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md` §5 in place of `ASK with SINGLE prompt`. Q2 marks Autonomous `(Recommended)`. The first Q-Exec option marks Native `(Recommended, default)`. |\n209\t| REQ-011 | The drift rows are cleared. `ask the council`, `convene` and `several models` leave `DEPTH_WORDING`, and the `several models` boost leaves `explicit.ts`, so H3b no longer tops `system-deep-loop`. The research aliases `iterative research`, `multi-round research` and `autonomous research` reach `hub-router.json` and `ROUTER.md`, so K2 tops `system-deep-loop` on the research route. `comprehensive research` and `deep investigation` leave `deep-research/SKILL.md`. `audit spec folder` and `pre-release review` leave `deep-review/SKILL.md`. The `:auto` invoke form is attached, the Gate 2 line names the advisor CLI, and both examples use `=` flags. The hub `SKILL.md` names `/doctor:deep-loop`. |\n210\t| REQ-012 | The single-probe misses are recorded. N7, N9, D1, V7, H6 and A3 each appear in `command-prompts.jsonl` as a `near-miss` row, and no new guard is added for them. |\n211\t| REQ-013 | The deep-family holdouts are fresh. The three deep-family `holdout` rows are replaced by rows a separate worker writes after tuning. No builder reads a `holdout` row. |\n212\t| REQ-014 | N9 (\"summarize the research.md from the last deep research run\") carries no deep command after the build. This is kept apart from REQ-002 because D2 keeps \"deep research\" as a loop ask and D6 rules out a guard for N9. See Open Questions. |\n213\t| REQ-015 | A spelled-out refusal withholds the command. \"don't do deep research, just answer quickly\", \"never run deep research on this\", \"no need to run a deep review here\", \"I'm not asking for a deep review, just explain the bug\", \"no deep review, please; explain the bug\" and \"a deep review is not needed, just check the diff\" carry no `/deep:*` command, and \"do a deep review of the parser\" keeps `/deep:review`. |\n214\t| REQ-016 | A question about the loop carries no command. \"how many iterations does deep research run by default?\" and \"how many passes does the deep review do\" carry no `/deep:*` command. |\n215\t| REQ-017 | Spelling variants keep the command. \"run a deep-review of the auth module\" gets `/deep:review`, and \"I’d like a research loop on cache eviction policies\", with a curly apostrophe, gets `/deep:research`. |\n216\t| REQ-018 | A negated symptom is not a stuck run. \"the deep research run is not stuck, run 5 more iterations\" gets `/deep:research`, not `/doctor:deep-loop`. |\n217\t| REQ-019 | A loop name that names the loop's own code or results, and a count that describes a subject, carry no command (D2 as narrowed by ADR-004). \"refactor the deep research scorer\", \"fix the bugs the deep review found\", \"open the review loop config\", \"we need a review loop for every PR\", \"I want a review loop that approves PRs automatically\", \"compare 10 iterations of the model and review the results\", \"research three-pass vs two-pass compilers\", \"several passes of the linter failed, review the config\" and \"review our multi-pass compiler\" carry no `/deep:*` command. \"run a deep review on the parser\", \"do 5 research iterations on caching\" and \"review the parser in several passes\" keep theirs. |\n218\t| REQ-020 | The Python typed-command check agrees with the TypeScript one. For \"don't run /deep:review, explain the review loop\", \"what does /deep:review do?\", \"see (/deep:review.md) for the flags\" and \"my deep review run is stuck, /deep:review again\", `_apply_deep_loop_offer_gate` with a typed row returns what `attachCommand` returns. |\n219\t| REQ-021 | Nothing earlier regresses. Every REQ-015 to REQ-020 prompt is in the shared fixture, both suites pass, the TypeScript and Python predicate comparison shows drift 0, every gain, keep and stage-one line of the 69-probe rerun keeps its command, and the corpus `false_offer` count stays 0. |\n220\t| REQ-022 | The docs say what was measured. The v4.2.0.0 changelog no longer says refused asks are skipped before they are, names packet 013's brief change and quotes the final suite count, and AC-008 reads `Waived` with ADR-003. |\n221\t\n222\t### Reopened after a fresh review\n223\t\n224\tA fresh review on 2026-11-23 found gate gaps outside the probe set. Six of them, reproduced through the Claude prompt hook at `a5d054a2f1c`:\n225\t\n226\t```text\n227\t[don't do deep research, just answer quickly] => use system-deep-loop → /deep:research (ask: A /deep:research:auto (Recommended), B /deep:research:confirm, C no loop) 0.90/0.12 pass.\n228\t[no need to run a deep review here] => ambiguous: system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask: A /deep:review:auto (Recommended), B /deep:review:confirm, C no loop) 0.95/0.16 vs sk-code 0.90/0.12 pass.\n229\t[/deep:review:confirm the auth module] => use system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask: A /deep:review:auto (Recommended), B /deep:review:confirm, C no loop) 0.94/0.12 pass."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:45:32.985Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.claude/projects/-Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-533-deep-loop-offers-deep-review/5edb1689-a87f-44c5-a1c5-441ad7fbf288/tool-results/bua6efjdm.txt","content":"<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\nThe advisor attaches `/deep:research` or `/deep:review` only when a prompt carries depth wording, so a request that asks for the loop in plain words gets no command row. In the block below, V6, H1a, H1b, E1 and E3 all ask for a loop or for iterations and all print `cmd=-`. A request that only asks for effort gets a command it did not ask for. R7 (\"find out everything you can\") prints `cmd=/deep:research pol=ask`. When a row is offered, no document says what the one question holds, which suffix follows a yes or which flags fit. The setup form after a yes is a typed-letter menu with no recommended option. A finished or stuck run halts with a message that names neither `--extend` nor `/doctor:deep-loop`.\n\n### Purpose\nA deep-loop command is offered when, and only when, the request asks for the loop itself. The offer is one question whose recommended option runs `:auto` with flags composed from the request.\n\n### Decision this packet follows\nThe operator's decision of 2026-11-22 (`scratch/decisions.md`, row D2) narrows the gate to explicit loop asks. It supersedes the rule in `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md` (line 44, \"a deep loop is offered only when the prompt uses depth wording\"). A reader of that packet should treat its depth-wording rule as replaced by this one.\n\nAn explicit loop ask is any of these:\n- It names a deep loop, deep research, deep review, a research loop or a review loop.\n- It gives an iteration count, or says \"iterations\", \"iterative\" or \"iteratively\".\n- It says multi-pass, or multiple, several or many passes.\n- It types a `/deep:*` command.\n- It asks to continue, resume or extend a deep run.\n\nDepth words alone are not a loop ask: thorough, thoroughly, in depth, exhaustive, deep dive, everything you can, final verdict. The council words are not one either: ask the council, convene, several models.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\n\nRun from the repository root on 2026-11-22. `git status --short .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor` printed nothing before and after the run, so this is the advisor as committed at `2ef3895f753`. The probe file holds 69 prompts taken from the routing analysis, grouped by what this packet expects of each. Every one exited 0 with `live` freshness.\n\n```text\n$ node specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/scratch/probes/probe.mjs specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/scratch/probes/probes-spec-baseline.json specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/scratch/probes/results-spec-baseline.json\nV6 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | system-deep-loop c=0.9471 u=0.12 route/single/review cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: sk-code c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: system-spec-kit c=0.82\nH1a [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=true | system-deep-loop c=0.95 u=0.16 route/single/review cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: sk-doc c=0.9449 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-code c=0.9316\nH1b [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | system-deep-loop c=0.9008 u=0.12 route/single/research cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: system-spec-kit c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: mcp-tooling c=0.82\nE1 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=true | system-deep-loop c=0.82 u=0.2 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill FLOORED || 2: cli-external-orchestration c=0.819 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-code c=0.82\nE3 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=true | system-deep-loop c=0.8756 u=0.16 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: cli-external-orchestration c=0.8746 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-code c=0.8651\nR2 [exit 0 live] n=1 amb=false | system-spec-kit c=0.82 u=0.18 -/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill FLOORED\nV2 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | sk-code c=0.95 u=0.12 route/single/sk-code-review cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: sk-git c=0.8435 cmd=- pol=- || 3: system-deep-loop c=0.82\nV4 [exit 0 live] n=1 amb=false | sk-code c=0.82 u=0.16 route/single/sk-code-review cmd=- pol=- kind=skill FLOORED\nH7 [exit 0 live] n=0 amb=false | NONE\nH10 [exit 0 live] n=1 amb=false | sk-code c=0.82 u=0.16 route/single/sk-code-review cmd=- pol=- kind=skill FLOORED\nR7 [exit 0 live] n=2 amb=true | system-deep-loop c=0.8545 u=0.16 route/single/research cmd=/deep:research pol=ask kind=skill || 2: sk-code c=0.8349 cmd=- pol=-\nN9 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | system-deep-loop c=0.9073 u=0.12 route/single/research cmd=/deep:research pol=ask kind=skill || 2: cli-external-orchestration c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-doc c=0.82\nV3 [exit 0 live] n=2 amb=true | system-deep-loop c=0.8619 u=0.16 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill needsMode || 2: system-spec-kit c=0.8261 cmd=- pol=-\nV8 [exit 0 live] n=2 amb=true | system-deep-loop c=0.95 u=0.16 defer/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill needsMode || 2: sk-code c=0.95 cmd=- pol=-\nV5 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | sk-code c=0.95 u=0.12 route/single/sk-code-review cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: system-deep-loop c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-doc c=0.82\nR2b [exit 0 live] n=1 amb=false | system-spec-kit c=0.8336 u=0.18 -/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill\nR3 [exit 0 live] n=2 amb=false | system-skill-advisor c=0.82 u=0.2 -/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill FLOORED || 2: system-spec-kit c=0.82 cmd=- pol=-\nR3b [exit 0 live] n=0 amb=false | NONE\nR6 [exit 0 live] n=0 amb=false | NONE\nA1 [exit 0 live] n=0 amb=false | NONE\nA4 [exit 0 live] n=0 amb=false | NONE\nA8 [exit 0 live] n=0 amb=false | NONE\nH6 [exit 0 live] n=2 amb=false | sk-doc c=0.8866 u=0.12 route/single/sk-create-quality-control cmd=- pol=- kind=skill || 2: sk-code c=0.82 cmd=- pol=-\nH8 [exit 0 live] n=1 amb=false | system-spec-kit c=0.82 u=0.16 -/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill FLOORED\nH9 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | system-spec-kit c=0.82 u=0.22 -/-/- cmd=- pol=- kind=skill FLOORED || 2: cli-external-orchestration c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-doc c=0.82\nR1 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=false | system-deep-loop c=0.9407 u=0.12 route/single/research cmd=/deep:research pol=ask kind=skill || 2: cli-external-orchestration c=0.82 cmd=- pol=- || 3: system-spec-kit c=0.82\nR5 [exit 0 live] n=1 amb=false | system-deep-loop c=0.9089 u=0.12 route/single/research cmd=/deep:research pol=ask kind=skill\nV1 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=true | system-deep-loop c=0.95 u=0.12 route/single/review cmd=/deep:review pol=ask kind=skill || 2: system-skill-advisor c=0.8838 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-code c=0.95\nE2 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=true | system-deep-loop c=0.9372 u=0.16 route/single/review cmd=/deep:review pol=ask kind=skill || 2: cli-external-orchestration c=0.9362 cmd=- pol=- || 3: sk-doc c=0.9006\nE4 [exit 0 live] n=3 amb=true | system-deep-loop c=0.881 u=0.12 route/single/research cmd=/deep:research pol=