{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013uFGL65bLzGwQtfZjxkqrr","type":"tool_result","content":"229\t[/deep:review:confirm the auth module] => use system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask: A /deep:review:auto (Recommended), B /deep:review:confirm, C no loop) 0.94/0.12 pass.\n230\t[run a deep-review of the auth module] => use system-deep-loop 0.95/0.12 pass.\n231\t[how many iterations does deep research run by default?] => use system-deep-loop → /deep:research (ask: A /deep:research:auto (Recommended), B /deep:research:confirm, C no loop) 0.93/0.12 pass.\n232\t[the deep research run is not stuck, run 5 more iterations] => use system-deep-loop → /doctor:deep-loop (run) 0.93/0.12 pass.\n233\t```\n234\t\n235\tThe typed-suffix hint is packet 013's to fix. REQ-015 to REQ-022 cover the rest.\n236\t\n237\t> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n238\t> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n239\t<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n240\t\n241\t---\n242\t\n243\t<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n244\t## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n245\t\n246\t- **SC-001**: Plain loop asks with a command row go from 0 of 5 to 5 of 5 on the gain group (V6, H1a, H1b, E1, E3) of the probe rerun.\n247\t- **SC-002**: Depth-only false offers go from 1 to 0. R7 is the one case, and no row in the no-gain group gains a `/deep:*` command.\n248\t- **SC-003**: The keep and negative groups, 34 rows in all, print the same top skill and `cmd=` value as the baseline block.\n249\t- **SC-005**: Every REQ-015 to REQ-020 prompt gives its stated result through the prompt hook, with the 69-probe and corpus results unchanged.\n250\t- **SC-004**: The recaptured routing baseline's `false_offer` and `false_offer_attached` counts, taken over the rows that existed before this packet, equal the counts captured before the code change.\n251\t<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n252\t\n253\t---\n254\t\n255\t<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n256\t## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n257\t\n258\t| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n259\t|------|------|--------|------------|\n260\t| Dependency | The rebuilt advisor `dist`. The CLI shim refuses a stale one | Every probe and corpus check fails without it | Rebuild with `npm run build` in the advisor runtime, then confirm the probe run prints `live` |\n261\t| Risk | The stage-one rule in `explicit.ts` scores every prompt on every runtime | High: a new rule can move an unrelated top skill | The negative group and the corpus recapture both gate it. Reject the change if any REQ-004 id moves |\n262\t| Risk | A new hub alias pulls an unrelated prompt | Medium: an earlier \"research run\" alias did this | Replay each new alias against an out-of-domain phrase, per `.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md` §4 |\n263\t| Risk | The near-miss rows raise the corpus false-offer totals by construction. N7 and D1 still put a command bridge in the top three (`false_offer`), and N9, D1 and V7 still attach or carry a command (`false_offer_attached`), with no guard | Low: the count reads as a regression | Compare the counts over the rows that existed before. Record the new rows' outcome on their own |\n264\t<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n265\t\n266\t---\n267\t\n268\t<!-- ANCHOR:nfr -->\n269\t## L2: NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n270\t\n271\t### Performance\n272\t- **NFR-P01**: The gate and the stage-one rule add only in-memory regular-expression tests, with no file or network I/O.\n273\t- **NFR-P02**: N/A for throughput. The advisor serves one prompt per call.\n274\t\n275\t### Security\n276\t- **NFR-S01**: The `run` policy never starts a deep command. Both `/deep` commands keep `ask`, as their `ask_first: [\"spend\"]` metadata derives.\n277\t- **NFR-S02**: N/A for data protection. No credential or user data is read or written.\n278\t\n279\t### Reliability\n280\t- **NFR-R01**: All 69 probes exit 0 with `live` freshness on the rerun, as they do in the baseline block.\n281\t- **NFR-R02**: The whole advisor vitest suite passes with zero failures.\n282\t<!-- /ANCHOR:nfr -->\n283\t\n284\t---\n285\t\n286\t<!-- ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n287\t## L2: EDGE CASES\n288\t\n289\t- Empty input: a prompt with no loop ask and no depth word, such as N10 (\"how does the deep loop decide to stop?\"), carries no command, as it does today.\n290\t- Maximum input: at the attach step, a prompt that holds both a loop ask and a depth word opens the gate on the loop ask. A prompt that names both research and review cues does not resolve a deferred route, so it carries no command. Both are unit cases in `command-attach.vitest.ts`, because whether such a prompt reaches the hub at all is the scorer's call.\n291\t- Failure path: a refusal to run, such as N6 (\"don't run /deep:review\"), carries no command. The no-edit guard holds before the mode-cue path.\n292\t<!-- /ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n293\t\n294\t---\n295\t\n296\t<!-- ANCHOR:complexity -->\n297\t## L2: COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n298\t\n299\t| Dimension | Score | Notes |\n300\t|-----------|-------|-------|\n301\t| Scope | 16/25 | About 20 files across the advisor runtime, two commands and one hub. The code change is two TypeScript files. |\n302\t| Risk | 15/25 | A scoring lane that every prompt passes through, on every runtime |\n303\t| Research | 6/20 | Done. 84 probes in `scratch/routing-analysis.md` and the baseline block above |\n304\t| **Total** | **37/70** | **Level 2** |\n305\t<!-- /ANCHOR:complexity -->\n306\t\n307\t---\n308\t\n309\t<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n310\t## 10. OPEN QUESTIONS\n311\t\n312\t- N9 names \"deep research\", which D2 keeps as a loop ask, and D6 rules out a guard for it. REQ-014 asks that N9 lose its command, but nothing in the five lanes is designed to drop it. If the rerun still shows `cmd=/deep:research` on N9, the operator decides between a waiver recorded in `decision-record.md` and a narrower reading of \"names deep research\", such as requiring a run verb.\n313\t- K3 (\"start an autonomous research session ... let it run overnight\") carries the new alias `autonomous research` but no D2 loop ask. Should it gain the command? The packet assumes no, so K3 is recorded and not required.\n314\t<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n315\t\n316\t---\n317\t\n318\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:45:38.618Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.claude/projects/-Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-533-deep-loop-offers-deep-review/5edb1689-a87f-44c5-a1c5-441ad7fbf288/tool-results/bua6efjdm.txt","content":"[/deep:review:confirm the auth module] => use system-deep-loop → /deep:review (ask: A /deep:review:auto (Recommended), B /deep:review:confirm, C no loop) 0.94/0.12 pass.\n[run a deep-review of the auth module] => use system-deep-loop 0.95/0.12 pass.\n[how many iterations does deep research run by default?] => use system-deep-loop → /deep:research (ask: A /deep:research:auto (Recommended), B /deep:research:confirm, C no loop) 0.93/0.12 pass.\n[the deep research run is not stuck, run 5 more iterations] => use system-deep-loop → /doctor:deep-loop (run) 0.93/0.12 pass.\n```\n\nThe typed-suffix hint is packet 013's to fix. REQ-015 to REQ-022 cover the rest.\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: Plain loop asks with a command row go from 0 of 5 to 5 of 5 on the gain group (V6, H1a, H1b, E1, E3) of the probe rerun.\n- **SC-002**: Depth-only false offers go from 1 to 0. R7 is the one case, and no row in the no-gain group gains a `/deep:*` command.\n- **SC-003**: The keep and negative groups, 34 rows in all, print the same top skill and `cmd=` value as the baseline block.\n- **SC-005**: Every REQ-015 to REQ-020 prompt gives its stated result through the prompt hook, with the 69-probe and corpus results unchanged.\n- **SC-004**: The recaptured routing baseline's `false_offer` and `false_offer_attached` counts, taken over the rows that existed before this packet, equal the counts captured before the code change.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | The rebuilt advisor `dist`. The CLI shim refuses a stale one | Every probe and corpus check fails without it | Rebuild with `npm run build` in the advisor runtime, then confirm the probe run prints `live` |\n| Risk | The stage-one rule in `explicit.ts` scores every prompt on every runtime | High: a new rule can move an unrelated top skill | The negative group and the corpus recapture both gate it. Reject the change if any REQ-004 id moves |\n| Risk | A new hub alias pulls an unrelated prompt | Medium: an earlier \"research run\" alias did this | Replay each new alias against an out-of-domain phrase, per `.skilled/repo-rules/skill-hub-routing.md` §4 |\n| Risk | The near-miss rows raise the corpus false-offer totals by construction. N7 and D1 still put a command bridge in the top three (`false_offer`), and N9, D1 and V7 still attach or carry a command (`false_offer_attached`), with no guard | Low: the count reads as a regression | Compare the counts over the rows that existed before. Record the new rows' outcome on their own |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:nfr -->\n## L2: NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: The gate and the stage-one rule add only in-memory regular-expression tests, with no file or network I/O.\n- **NFR-P02**: N/A for throughput. The advisor serves one prompt per call.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: The `run` policy never starts a deep command. Both `/deep` commands keep `ask`, as their `ask_first: [\"spend\"]` metadata derives.\n- **NFR-S02**: N/A for data protection. No credential or user data is read or written.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: All 69 probes exit 0 with `live` freshness on the rerun, as they do in the baseline block.\n- **NFR-R02**: The whole advisor vitest suite passes with zero failures.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:nfr -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n## L2: EDGE CASES\n\n- Empty input: a prompt with no loop ask and no depth word, such as N10 (\"how does the deep loop decide to stop?\"), carries no command, as it does today.\n- Maximum input: at the attach step, a prompt that holds both a loop ask and a depth word opens the gate on the loop ask. A prompt that names both research and review cues does not resolve a deferred route, so it carries no command. Both are unit cases in `command-attach.vitest.ts`, because whether such a prompt reaches the hub at all is the scorer's call.\n- Failure path: a refusal to run, such as N6 (\"don't run /deep:review\"), carries no command. The no-edit guard holds before the mode-cue path.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:complexity -->\n## L2: COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Notes |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Scope | 16/25 | About 20 files across the advisor runtime, two commands and one hub. The code change is two TypeScript files. |\n| Risk | 15/25 | A scoring lane that every prompt passes through, on every runtime |\n| Research | 6/20 | Done. 84 probes in `scratch/routing-analysis.md` and the baseline block above |\n| **Total** | **37/70** | **Level 2** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:complexity -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 10. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- N9 names \"deep research\", which D2 keeps as a loop ask, and D6 rules out a guard for it. REQ-014 asks that N9 lose its command, but nothing in the five lanes is designed to drop it. If the rerun still shows `cmd=/deep:research` on N9, the operator decides between a waiver recorded in `decision-record.md` and a narrower reading of \"names deep research\", such as requiring a run verb.\n- K3 (\"start an autonomous research session ... let it run overnight\") carries the new alias `autonomous research` but no D2 loop ask. Should it gain the command? The packet assumes no, so K3 is recorded and not required.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n","numLines":90,"startLine":229,"totalLines":318}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013uFGL65bLzGwQtfZjxkqrr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
