{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QGsZLBc6YzXz5uibe6RjZx","type":"tool_result","content":"     115 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/acceptance-criteria.md\n     260 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/tasks.md\n     230 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/012-deep-loop-command-offers/implementation-summary.md\n     605 total\n31:> every row below is `Met`, `Waived` or `Superseded`. A `Waived` or `Superseded`\n50:<!-- FILL: Write one row per requirement. The Then clause names a command. GOOD: AC-001: When `--keep 3` runs, Then `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3. WEAK: The feature works. -->\n58:| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given the rebuilt advisor, When V6, H1a, H1b, E1 and E3 are probed, Then the top row is `system-deep-loop` with `cmd=/deep:review pol=ask` on V6, H1a and E3 and `cmd=/deep:research pol=ask` on H1b and E1 | `PROBE`, the five gain lines. Observed 2026-11-23 in `scratch/probes/results-after.json`: V6, H1a and E3 top `system-deep-loop` with `cmd=/deep:review pol=ask`, and H1b and E1 with `cmd=/deep:research pol=ask`. Evidence: `implementation-summary.md:155`. | Met | - |\n59:| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given the rebuilt advisor, When R7 is probed, Then its top row prints `cmd=-` | `PROBE`, the R7 line. Observed 2026-11-23: R7 prints `cmd=-`. Evidence: `implementation-summary.md:155`. | Met | - |\n60:| AC-003 | REQ-002 | Given the rebuilt advisor, When V3, V8, V5, R2b, R3, R3b, R6, A1, A4, A8, H6, H8 and H9 are probed, Then no row of any of them carries a `/deep:*` command, and V5's top row is still `sk-code` on `sk-code-review` | `PROBE`, the no-gain lines. Observed 2026-11-23: none of the thirteen carries a `/deep:*` command in its three rows, and V5 tops `sk-code` on `sk-code-review`. Evidence: `implementation-summary.md:155`. | Met | - |\n61:| AC-004 | REQ-003 | Given the rebuilt advisor, When the seventeen keep rows are probed, Then each prints the same `/deep:*` command and `pol=ask` as the baseline | `PROBE`, the keep lines compared with `results-spec-baseline.json`. Observed 2026-11-23: all seventeen print the baseline command and `pol=ask`. Evidence: `implementation-summary.md:155`. | Met | - |\n62:| AC-005 | REQ-004 | Given the rebuilt advisor, When the seventeen negative rows are probed, Then each prints the same top skill and the same `cmd=` value as the baseline | `PROBE`, the negative lines compared with `results-spec-baseline.json`. Observed 2026-11-23: all seventeen print the baseline top skill and `cmd=` value. Evidence: `implementation-summary.md:155`. | Met | - |\n63:| AC-006 | REQ-005 | Given both deep presentation files, When they are searched, Then each holds `### Offer From an Advisor Brief`, a recommended option A that runs `:auto` with `--spec-folder=<the Gate 3 answer>`, option B on `:confirm`, option C with no loop, a native executor unless one is named, and fan-out only on two or more named executors or independent takes | `rg -n 'Offer From an Advisor Brief\\|:auto\\|--spec-folder=<the Gate 3 answer>\\|:confirm' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt`, then a read of each section. Observed 2026-11-23: one heading per file, and each section holds A) Run it (Recommended) with `:auto` and `--spec-folder=<the Gate 3 answer>`, B) `:confirm`, C) no loop, the native executor by default and fan-out only on two or more named executors or independent takes. Evidence: `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt:13`. | Met | - |\n64:| AC-007 | REQ-005 | Given both command documents, When MODE ROUTING is read, Then step 0 points at the offer section and counts a missing advisor policy as `ask` | `rg -n 'Offer From an Advisor Brief' .skilled/commands/deep/research.md .skilled/commands/deep/review.md` prints one line per file. Observed 2026-11-23: one line per file. Evidence: `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:86`. | Met | - |\n65:| AC-008 | REQ-005 | Given a session on F3, F5 or F6, When the AI acts on the brief, Then its first visible response is one question whose recommended option carries the expected flag: fan-out groups, `--depth-mode=expansive` and `--extend=3` | Manual: one recorded session each through `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`. Observed 2026-11-23: the F3 and F5 recordings in `scratch/behaviour/` recommend the fan-out groups and the expansive run through the text fallback, because the headless session had no question tool, and a live TUI run showed the question-tool dialog. The first F6 recording answered another prompt and is kept as `scratch/behaviour/F6-other-prompt.md`. Three fresh runs on the F6 prompt each stopped before spending but none asked the offer with options A, B and C. In plan mode (`scratch/behaviour/F6-plan-mode.md`) the session composed `--extend=3` and submitted a plan. Outside plan mode (`scratch/behaviour/F6.md`) it asked the spec-folder question and named `--extend=3` as the command it would run. After step 0 of both command documents was made to name the three options (`scratch/behaviour/F6-after-step0.md`), it asked which review was meant before opening the command document. Three more samples after that edit split: sample 1 (`scratch/behaviour/F6-sample-1.md`) asked which packet and offered A) `/deep:review:auto --extend=3 --spec-folder=<path>` as the recommended option, B) `:confirm` and C) no loop, through the text fallback as F3 and F5 did, while samples 2 and 3 asked for the target first and deferred the command document. Since the edit, 1 of 4 runs asked the offer, and the operator accepted that as Met with the rate disclosed. Evidence: `scratch/behaviour/F6-sample-1.md:23`. | Waived | ADR-003 |\n66:| AC-009 | REQ-006 | Given the edited gate, When the unit file runs, Then every loop-ask clause returns its command and every depth word returns `undefined` | `npx vitest run tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` reports 0 failed. Observed 2026-11-23: the loop-ask and depth-word cases live in `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, beside the file named. With \"thoroughly\", \"exhaustive\" and \"deep dive\" added, the two files report 294 passed and 0 failed. Evidence: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:536`. | Met | - |\n67:| AC-010 | REQ-006 | Given the whole advisor suite and a rebuilt `dist`, When both run, Then the suite reports 0 failed and every probe line reads `exit 0 live` | `npx vitest run` and `npm run build` in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`, then `PROBE`. Observed 2026-11-23: `npm run build` exit 0, `npx vitest run` 180 files with 0 failed, and all 69 probe lines read `exit 0 live`. Evidence: `implementation-summary.md:156`. | Met | - |\n68:| AC-011 | REQ-007 | Given the edited command assets, When the mirror and reference gates run, Then both exit 0 and the compiled contracts no longer hold `ASK with SINGLE prompt` | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`; `node .skilled/commands/scripts/validate-command-references.cjs`; `rg -c 'ASK with SINGLE prompt' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/` prints nothing. Observed 2026-11-23: the mirror check passes 260 mirrors, command references resolve across 84 asset files, and the `rg` prints nothing. Evidence: `implementation-summary.md:156`. | Met | - |\n69:| AC-012 | REQ-007 | Given the corpus with the new rows, When the baseline is recaptured, Then `false_offer` and `false_offer_attached` over the rows that existed before equal the counts captured before the code change, and each new near-miss row's outcome is recorded on its own | `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` before and after, with both counts written into `implementation-summary.md`. Observed 2026-11-23: over the 35 rows that existed before the packet, `false_offer` and `false_offer_attached` are both 0, as in the baseline before the code change. The new rows are recorded in `implementation-summary.md`. Evidence: `implementation-summary.md:157`. | Met | - |\n70:| AC-013 | REQ-008 | Given the stage-one rule, When R2, V2, V4, H7 and H10 are probed, Then each id's top row is recorded, and no REQ-004 negative changes its top skill | `PROBE`, the stage-one lines quoted in `implementation-summary.md`. Observed 2026-11-23: R2 tops `system-spec-kit`, V2, V4 and H10 top `system-deep-loop` with `/deep:review`, H7 tops it with `/deep:research`, and no REQ-004 id changed its top skill. Evidence: `implementation-summary.md:155`. | Met | - |\n71:| AC-014 | REQ-009 | Given the edited YAML and presentation files, When they are searched, Then the completed-packet message names `--extend=N` and `--restart`, and both Next Steps tables and both `next_steps` lists carry `--extend=N` and a `/doctor:deep-loop --scope=` row | `rg -n -- '--extend=N\\|--restart\\|doctor:deep-loop --scope=' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-presentation.txt`. Observed 2026-11-23: each of the four files prints matching lines. Evidence: `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research.yaml:68`. | Met | - |\n72:| AC-015 | REQ-010 | Given both presentation files, When step 6, Q2 and Q-Exec are read, Then step 6 names the question tool from `communication-handoff.md` §5, Q2 marks Autonomous `(Recommended)` and Q-Exec marks Native `(Recommended, default)` | `rg -c 'ASK with SINGLE prompt'` prints 0 on both files; `rg -n 'communication-handoff.md\\|Autonomous \\(Recommended\\)\\|Native \\(Recommended, default\\)'` prints each in both. Observed 2026-11-23: `ASK with SINGLE prompt` is absent