ctually observed. |\n94:| `Waived` | Deliberately not pursued. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n99:Write `-` when the row is `Met` or `Unmet`. Write `ADR-NNN` when the row is\n100:`Waived` or `Superseded`, naming a decision record that exists in\n110:<!-- FILL: Write Yes or No and one sentence. Name a criterion by its id only when it blocks closure. Never write a count of criteria or an id range, because every added row makes it wrong. GOOD: No. AC-002 is unmet. WEAK: All eight criteria AC-001 to AC-008 are met. -->\n114:Every row is `Met`, `Waived` or `Superseded`, and each waiver and supersession names an ADR in `decision-record.md`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"unavailable":true}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QGsZLBc6YzXz5uibe6RjZx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
