w\", \"no deep review, please\" and \"a deep review is not needed\" carry no command. The gate now reads each loop phrase on its own and skips one that a refusal leads or that a need word after it turns down. \"why not run a deep review\" and \"no, run a deep review\" still ask.\n- **How many:** \"how many iterations does deep research run by default?\" and \"how many passes does the deep review do\" are questions about the loop.\n- **Spellings:** \"deep-review\" and \"deep-research\" count, except inside a path such as `deep-review.md`. A curly apostrophe reads as a straight one in the run-ask and write-about checks.\n- **Denied symptoms:** \"the deep research run is not stuck, run 5 more iterations\" gets `/deep:research`. A negation before a state word denies the symptom, and a counted run ask cancels the stuck reading unless a refusal leads it.\n- **Loop as subject (ADR-004):** an edit verb before the name, or a code, file or result noun or a result verb after it, makes the loop the subject. So do iterations of something that is not the loop, a count that did something (\"several passes of the linter failed\") and a hyphen count or `multi-pass` that describes another noun. A wanted loop \"for every PR\" or one \"that approves PRs\" is a standing process. Probe H10, \"a multi-pass security and correctness audit\", first lost its command, so up to three words may stand before the loop's noun.\n- **Python typed check:** the fallback now reads a typed `/deep:*` command with the TypeScript boundary rule, and it ports the ask-policy part of `commandOnlyMentioned`. A stuck run drops the run row even when the command is typed, as `attachCommand` does.\n\nWhat stays open:\n1. **The blind -04 holdouts score 2 of 3.**\n27:- Every executor builds one way, and a bad setup is refused before it runs.\n41:- Most overlay refusals name the next command.\n55:> 1. OpenCode 1 is no longer supported, and deep-loop runs refuse a major-1 binary. [OpenCode 2 only](#c-opencode-2-is-the-only-supported-major)\n59:> 5. `fanout-run.cjs --allow-single-lineage` is gone, and a one-lineage matrix is refused. [Rerun one lineage](#c-watch-stop-and-rerun-one-lineage)\n60:> 6. A fan-out lineage with the `native` executor kind is refused. [Rerun one lineage](#c-watch-stop-and-rerun-one-lineage)\n62:> 8. A finished DeepSeek Harness lineage that asked for `danger-full-access` is refused once on rerun. [Sandbox reports](#c-sandbox-reports-name-the-real-mode)\n64:> 10. Two dispatch setup refusals now exit 64, not 1. [Setup mistakes](#c-setup-mistakes-stop-before-dispatch)\n65:> 11. A manifest with a duplicate or escaping layout link now exits 2. [Layout links](#c-bad-layout-links-are-refused)\n66:> 12. `record-base --pin` refuses a commit with no `.skilled` folder. [Release base](#c-the-release-base-takes-only-a-framework-commit)\n117:| [Setup mistakes stop before dispatch](#c-setup-mistakes-stop-before-dispatch) | A bad artifact dir is refused before the executor runs. | Dispatch and Safety |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013ogpiRSJBTJDjXCpYuKZGS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
