{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMA8fvwHeuhFbJVkkQ6s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The opus-medium-3 lineage is finished. It ran all 5 iterations, one per dimension (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability) plus a second correctness pass. It found 1 P1 and 9 P2, and its derived verdict is **FAIL**.\n\nThe findings alone would give CONDITIONAL, since there is no P0 and one P1. FAIL comes from the coverage gate: both core traceability checks ended `partial` because of the gaps below. The evidence and scope gates passed, and the run stopped on `maxIterationsReached` as required.\n\n**The P1**\n- **The two paths disagree on a typed command in a stuck-run complaint.** For \"my deep review run is stuck, /deep:review again\", `attachCommand` returns `/doctor:deep-loop`, but `attachTypedCommand` (`advisor-recommend.ts:434`) then puts `/deep:review` back on the top row. The Python gate drops the run row instead. Acceptance criterion AC-027 says both paths withhold the command, but its test only checks `attachCommand` (`deep-loop-offer-cases.vitest.ts:57`). The operator needs to decide which behaviour is intended.\n\n**The P2s**\n- **Typed command lost:** typing `/deep:research` and a longer, unrelated command gives no command at all, because `typedCommandIn` keeps the longest name across all commands (`command-attach.ts:238`). Python disagrees.\n- **Offer shown on a typed command:** when the Python fallback serves the brief, the row never gets the `typed` flag. A typed `/deep:review:confirm` still shows the three offer options, which packet 013's REQ-006 rules out.\n- **Refusals missed:** \"skip\", \"avoid\", \"instead of\" and \"refuse\" don't withhold the deep command, in TypeScript or Python.\n- **Doctor offered against a refusal:** a stuck-run complaint that says \"please don't run anything\" still gets `/doctor:deep-loop`, which runs without asking.\n- **Python fallback slows down sharply on long prompts:** time grows with the square of prompt length. A 96,000-character prompt took 6.3 s, over the fallback's 3 s timeout.\n- **Wrong status text:** AC-008's evidence cell says the operator \"accepted that as Met\", but its status is `Waived`.\n- **Vocabulary copied by hand:** Python retypes the loop-phrase lists that TypeScript keeps as data. Only the shared test fixture's prompts catch drift between them.\n- **Review mode cue misses -ing forms:** \"checking\" or \"inspecting\" for bugs doesn't count as a review, though the code comment says it does.\n- **Scoring rule skips the gate's exceptions (unconfirmed):** the first-stage scoring rule in `explicit.ts:449` boosts the deep loop on loop words without the gate's subject and refusal checks. I inferred this from the code and didn't run the full scorer to confirm it.\n\n**What I did not run:** the `skill_advisor.py` CLI (it may write its cache outside the lineage), the full scorer, the probe suites and the test suites. I read Python behaviour from source and imported the module read-only. I probed the TypeScript gate by importing its source directly.\n\nEverything is in the lineage directory: five iteration files and deltas, `review-report.md`, the strategy and registry, and the terminal synthesis record. `git status` shows no tracked file changed, and the lock is released.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:opus-medium-3"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":354,"cache_read_input_tokens":257070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":354},"output_tokens":753,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:56:13.380Z","request_id":"<redacted>"}
